ity of life. \n\nPatients undergoing chemotherapy may experience complications such as oropharyngeal dysphagia, hyperglycemia, cachexia, nausea, vomiting, and mucositis, which can hinder normal food intake and may necessitate enteral nutrition. The treatment can also result in nutritional deficiencies and weight changes, including loss of appetite. As a result, careful management of the patient's nutritional needs is crucial during chemotherapy to mitigate these adverse effects and support recovery. \n\nIn summary, QUIMIOTERAPIA is a vital but challenging component of cancer treatment, requiring close attention to the patient's health and nutritional status throughout the process.\",23\r\n25,RADIOTERAPIA,\"RADIOTERAPIA, or radiotherapy, is a treatment method that employs high doses of radiation to eliminate cancer cells. It is frequently utilized in the management of neoplasms and may be considered as a treatment option following surgery. While effective in targeting cancer, radiotherapy can have significant adverse effects on a patient's nutritional status. These effects can manifest as acute and chronic nutritional complications, which are influenced by factors such as the tumor's location and the radiation dose administered.\n\nPatients undergoing radiotherapy may experience side effects like mucositis, which can hinder their ability to consume adequate nutrition. Additionally, the treatment can lead to oropharyngeal dysphagia, particularly in individuals with head and neck cancers, further complicating their nutritional intake. There is also a risk of damage to the pituitary gland, potentially resulting in hormonal deficiencies such as hypopituitarism.\n\nOverall, while RADIOTERAPIA is a critical component of cancer treatment, it is essential to monitor and manage the nutritional implications that arise during the course of therapy to ensure the well-being of patients.\",14\r\n2326,NPT,\"NPT, which stands for Nutrición Parenteral Total or Nutritional Parenteral Therapy, is a method of providing nutrition intravenously to patients who are unable to eat or absorb nutrients through their gastrointestinal tract. This nutritional support is particularly crucial for patients during their hospital stay and is also utilized for infants who cannot receive adequate nutrition through oral feeding. NPT is specifically indicated for individuals with conditions such as severe pancreatitis, where oral intake is not possible or tolerated. Overall, NPT serves as a vital intervention for those requiring nutritional support when traditional feeding methods are not feasible.\",13\r\n2321,MUCOSITIS,\"Mucositis is an inflammatory condition affecting the mucous membranes, particularly in the digestive tract, and is commonly induced by chemoradiotherapy in cancer patients. This condition is characterized by inflammation and ulceration of the mucous membranes, leading to significant complications such as dysphagia and difficulties with nutritional intake. It is reported that mucositis has a high incidence rate, occurring in approximately 70% of patients undergoing intensive chemotherapy treatments. \n\nThe condition can severely impact a patient's ability to eat, making nutritional intervention necessary. Mucositis is especially prevalent among patients receiving high-dose chemotherapy and those undergoing radiotherapy, including those who have undergone hematopoietic cell transplants. \n\nManagement strategies for mucositis may include the administration of oral glutamine, which has been shown to reduce the duration and severity of the condition. Overall, mucositis is a painful and challenging side effect of cancer treatments that requires careful attention to ensure adequate nutrition and patient comfort.\",17\r\n13635,PACIENTE NEOPLÁSICO,El paciente neoplásico es una persona diagnosticada con cáncer que enfrenta desafíos nutricionales y de salud debido a la enfermedad y sus tratamientos.,6\r\n13634,INMUNOTERAPIA,\"La inmunoterapia es un tratamiento que puede causar cansancio, náuseas y anorexia, y a menudo se combina con quimioterapia en casos avanzados.\",3\r\n13375,TERAPIA NEOADYUVANTE,\"La terapia neoadyuvante es un tratamiento previo a la cirugía que combina quimioterapia y/o radioterapia para tratar tumores esofágicos, pero puede afectar negativamente el estado nutricional de los pacientes.\",4\r\n8513,EFECTOS SECUNDARIOS,\"\"\"EFECTOS SECUNDARIOS\"\" refers to side effects that are a significant concern in the development of obesity treatments. These side effects can also be observed in other medical treatments, such as oncological therapies, where they manifest as symptoms like nausea and loss of appetite, which negatively impact the patient's nutrition. Additionally, side effects can arise from low-carbohydrate diets, leading to adverse reactions such as constipation and headaches. Overall, \"\"EFECTOS SECUNDARIOS\"\" encompasses a range of adverse reactions that can affect both obesity treatments and other medical interventions, highlighting the importance of monitoring and managing these effects to ensure patient well-being.\",4\r\n2329,APLASIA MEDULAR,\"Condición que se presenta en el postrasplante inmediato, relacionada con la reducción de células sanguíneas.\",1\r\n12622,FISTULAS DE ALTO DÉBITO,FISTULAS DE ALTO DÉBITO are medical conditions that may necessitate specialized nutritional support due to high output.,1\r\n12623,OBSTRUCCIÓN DIGESTIVA PARCIAL,OBSTRUCCIÓN DIGESTIVA PARCIAL is a condition that can affect nutrient absorption and may require nutritional intervention.,1\r\n13376,MORBILIDAD PERIOPERATORIA,\"La morbilidad perioperatoria se refiere a las complicaciones que pueden ocurrir alrededor del tiempo de una cirugía, especialmente en pacientes con cáncer esofágico.\",1\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n888,QUIMIOTERAPIA,PACIENTE,\"The patient underwent chemotherapy as part of their cancer treatment, which led to various sid